,title,link,text,language,family
0,Yugambeh people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yugambeh_people,"It tells of the arrival to this part of the eastern Australian coastline by 3 men/mythical culture heroes (Berruġ, Mommóm and Yaburóng)and their wives and children in a canoe.",Minjungbal,Australian
1,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"Contemporary fusions of indigenous and Western styles are exemplified in the works of Yothu Yindi, No Fixed Address, Geoffrey Gurrumul Yunupingu and Christine Anu, and mark distinctly Australian contributions to world music.",Minjungbal,Australian
2,Minjungbal Museum & Cultural Centre,https://minjungbalmuseum.com.au/,"Now considered to be one of Australia’s most beautiful National Parks, take a stroll along the Tweed River, cutting through bushland and mangroves to discover the flora, fauna, bush tucker and culture of the Minjungbal people.",Minjungbal,Australian
3,The Minjungbal Aboriginal Cultural Centre in Tweed Heads ...,https://www.baysider.com/Business/Minjungbal_Aboriginal_Cultural_Centre/,"The Minjungbal Aboriginal Cultural Centre is a Tweed Heads historical site, and the ideal place to learn about Aboriginal culture, listen to Aboriginal music and enjoy a picnic or BBQ, it's great for school excursions and day trips.",Minjungbal,Australian
4,Museum Collections - Minjungbal Museum & Cultural Centre,https://minjungbalmuseum.com.au/museum-collections/,"Exhibits will engage you with the history of the local area and Aboriginal people, while informative videos provide insight into our traditional culture. You may even catch some song or dance performances on our outdoor stage. These traditional tools were found in the Cudgen area about 80 years ago by a local farmer.",Minjungbal,Australian
5,Natalie Gauci - Ambassador — National Survivors' Day,https://www.nationalsurvivorsday.org.au/natalie,"Natalie lives on the land of the Minjungbal people. Natalie Gauci is an award-winning Australian singer-songwriter whose music is celebrated for its raw honesty, intimacy, and emotional power.",Minjungbal,Australian
6,Bundjalung Kunjiel - Elementary Festival,https://elementaryfestival.co.uk/bundjalung-kunjiel/,"Mainly from Kombumerri, Minjungbal, and Nunukal knowledge holders but also teachers from central Australia and the top end of Queensland. Bundjalung Kunjiel has represented their community by showcasing songs and dances for Aboriginal family gatherings, public and private events.",Minjungbal,Australian
